meta {
  name: 02 Get usage
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/usage
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.seatsUsed: eq 0
  res.body.seatsLimit: eq 3
  res.body.seatsAvailable: eq 3
}

docs {
  A seat is a student row carrying this center id. Usage is counted on every
  read rather than stored in a column, so there is no counter that can drift
  away from the students it claims to describe.

  Nothing can provision students until Phase 4, so `seatsUsed` is 0 here. To
  exercise it now, set `center_id` on a student row in the database and re-run:
  the count moves immediately.

  Two things to verify by hand:

  - Students of a DIFFERENT center must never appear in this count. Point a
    second center's students at that center and confirm this number ignores
    them.

  - `seatsAvailable` must never go negative. Give the center more students than
    `seatsLimit` and it reports 0, not a deficit. Being over the limit blocks
    future provisioning; it does not evict anyone, and existing students keep
    working.
}
